<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>IRC channel logs</title><style>html {
  background: #fdfdfd;
}

h1 {
  font-weight: 300;
}

h2 {
  font-weight: 200;
}

h3 {
  padding: .5em 0;
  border-top: 3px dotted #ddd;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

form {
  width: 400px;
  display: flex;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  border-radius: .25em 0 0 .25em;
  border: 1px solid #aaa;
  border-right: 0;
  padding: 0.5em;
}

button {
  display: flex;
  border-radius: 0 .25em .25em 0;
  background-color: #007bff;
  border: 1px solid #007bff;
  padding: .5em;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: white;
}

button:hover {
  background-color: #0069d9;
  border-color: #0062cc;
}

a {
  color: #007bff;
  text-decoration: none;
}

a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

h4 {
  margin-bottom: .5em;
}

table td {
  padding: 0.75em;
}

table tr:hover {
  background: #eee;
}

.year {
  display: table;
}

.month {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-right: 1em;
}

ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.nick {
  padding-right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: right;
  width: 13rem;
  display: table-cell;
}

.nick a {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.message {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-left: 0.6rem;
  border-left: 2px solid #333;
}

.notice {
  color: #859900;
  font-style: italic;
}

.line {
  line-height: 1.8rem;
  display: table;
}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-12-15.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="000219"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#000219" label="[00:02:19]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it's mostly gnulib that uses snapshots</span></div><div class="line" id="000228"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#000228" label="[00:02:28]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and possibly a couple of other tarballs</span></div><div class="line" id="000933"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#000933" label="[00:09:33]">&lt;lanodan&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Well github/codeberg/… autogenerated tarballs have the same kind of problem as any kind of snapshot though</span></div><div class="line" id="001242"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#001242" label="[00:12:42]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">true</span></div><div class="line" id="001257"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#001257" label="[00:12:57]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">though release tarballs have another problem, they are usually full of generated code :(</span></div><div class="line" id="001404"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#001404" label="[00:14:04]">&lt;lanodan&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yeah :(</span></div><div class="line" id="014808"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#014808" label="[01:48:08]">&lt;Googulator&gt;</a></span><span class="message">fossy: probably OK as a stopgap, but obviously not a full long-term fix</span></div><div class="line" id="014916"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#014916" label="[01:49:16]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">perhaps contacting Savannah people might make sense?</span></div><div class="line" id="014923"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#014923" label="[01:49:23]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">to ask why it was removed...</span></div><div class="line" id="014931"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#014931" label="[01:49:31]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it might also be unintentional</span></div><div class="line" id="014944"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#014944" label="[01:49:44]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">e.g. happened during some upgrade</span></div><div class="line" id="021334"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#021334" label="[02:13:34]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yeah, that would be sensible</span></div><div class="line" id="021347"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#021347" label="[02:13:47]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">if they did it on purpose i have no idea what a long-term fix would be :\</span></div><div class="line" id="022719"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#022719" label="[02:27:19]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">hmm, actually we could do it through gitweb instead of cgit, they haven't disabled .tar.gz downloads there</span></div><div class="line" id="023308"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#023308" label="[02:33:08]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">fossy: are hashes different?</span></div><div class="line" id="023605"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#023605" label="[02:36:05]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and what are the URLs, e.g. for gnulib?</span></div><div class="line" id="023618"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#023618" label="[02:36:18]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I get project listing disabled here: <a rel="nofollow" href="https://git.savannah.gnu.org/gitweb/">https://git.savannah.gnu.org/gitweb/</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="035904"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#035904" label="[03:59:04]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> <a rel="nofollow" href="https://git.savannah.gnu.org/gitweb/?p=gnulib.git;a=commit;h=2e8033f55cbe31f49db6e78f2b9d15f2677bde90">https://git.savannah.gnu.org/gitweb/?p=gnulib.git;a=commit;h=2e8033f55cbe31f49db6e78f2b9d15f2677bde90</a>  e.g.</span></div><div class="line" id="040023"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#040023" label="[04:00:23]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ya, same checksums</span></div><div class="line" id="040036"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#040036" label="[04:00:36]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">the urls are reallly ugly though, but whatever</span></div><div class="line" id="150545"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#150545" label="[15:05:45]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">nice, after sanitizing musl-libc for linux-2.4 ABI and patching a few dozen builds almost everything seems to work: vis-editor, gdb, htop shows processes now</span></div><div class="line" id="150633"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#150633" label="[15:06:33]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">with yaft terminal there's some decent unicode support</span></div><div class="line" id="150647"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#150647" label="[15:06:47]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">that was a two-year hackjob to get it done</span></div><div class="line" id="183253"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#183253" label="[18:32:53]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">lanodan: i am aware of the problems with coreboot relying upon gnu dependency graph</span></div><div class="line" id="183431"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#183431" label="[18:34:31]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ekaitz: however, even when risc-v support progressed for any type of POSIX that needs bootstrapping, if risc-v dependency graph was not sanitizied and continued to rely upon x86_32</span></div><div class="line" id="183539"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#183539" label="[18:35:39]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">bootstrapping problems accumulate, because risc-v (or arm) rely upon x86 bootstrapping/crossdev plus all the problems that risc-v build-time dependency graph may or may not introduce atop</span></div><div class="line" id="183624"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#183624" label="[18:36:24]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">hence it's moot pointing to x86 bootstrapping issues to justifiy risc-v if x86 could not be avoided anayway</span></div><div class="line" id="183829"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#183829" label="[18:38:29]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">furthermore, even when UEFI firmware would hide 16bit real-mode with or without proprietary malice, then this doesn't mean the related bootstrapping issues of 16bit real-mode would be absent</span></div><div class="line" id="184051"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#184051" label="[18:40:51]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&quot;you should only need an uefi bootloader&quot;... that circuumvents the question how the the UEFI subsystem malice got introduced</span></div><div class="line" id="184235"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#184235" label="[18:42:35]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">similar to 16bit x86 BIOS which remains an open issue indefinitely, UEFI just adds malice atop of it</span></div><div class="line" id="184245"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#184245" label="[18:42:45]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&quot;you should only need an uefi bootloader&quot;</span></div><div class="line" id="184303"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#184303" label="[18:43:03]">&lt;aggi&gt;</a></span><span class="message">this doesn't solve any problems, it introduces even more</span></div><div class="line" id="220841"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#220841" label="[22:08:41]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">kpcyrd: hi, in May you had a question about ruby and pregenerated files</span></div><div class="line" id="220843"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#220843" label="[22:08:43]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">still interested?</span></div><div class="line" id="221015"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#221015" label="[22:10:15]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I've spend a couple of hours on that and had some success</span></div><div class="line" id="224227"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#224227" label="[22:42:27]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, I've got toe the latest ruby, without too much difficulty...</span></div><div class="line" id="224953"><span class="nick" style="color:#6d2462"><a href="#224953" label="[22:49:53]">&lt;kpcyrd&gt;</a></span><span class="message">stikonas: May is a while back, I don't remember the question. happy to hear the answer though. :)</span></div><div class="line" id="225135"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#225135" label="[22:51:35]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">question was here: <a rel="nofollow" href="https://logs.guix.gnu.org/bootstrappable/2024-05-10.log">https://logs.guix.gnu.org/bootstrappable/2024-05-10.log</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="225218"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#225218" label="[22:52:18]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and this is the way to avoid using those pregenerated files: <a rel="nofollow" href="https://stikonas.eu/files/bootstrap/ruby_bootstrap.txt">https://stikonas.eu/files/bootstrap/ruby_bootstrap.txt</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="225250"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#225250" label="[22:52:50]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(I'm not claiming this is the shortest way but that worked for me)</span></div><div class="line" id="231016"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#231016" label="[23:10:16]">&lt;lanodan&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Is there a reason for bison-2.3?</span></div><div class="line" id="231456"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231456" label="[23:14:56]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I needed some older bison</span></div><div class="line" id="231505"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231505" label="[23:15:05]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">so I just grabbed something old from live-bootstrap</span></div><div class="line" id="231523"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#231523" label="[23:15:23]">&lt;lanodan&gt;</a></span><span class="message">makes sense</span></div><div class="line" id="231524"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231524" label="[23:15:24]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">by current bison 3.8 was not compatible with those</span></div><div class="line" id="231537"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231537" label="[23:15:37]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">perhaps it created .c and .h files but they failed to compile</span></div><div class="line" id="231605"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231605" label="[23:16:05]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and I've just tried to skip 2.2 completely, but that doesn't work</span></div><div class="line" id="231619"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231619" label="[23:16:19]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">ruby 2.7 does not build with ruby 1.8.5</span></div><div class="line" id="231649"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231649" label="[23:16:49]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, 2.2 has this bison annoyance, 2.7 then has an annoying issue with openssl (it requires it but openssl 3 is not supported)</span></div><div class="line" id="231656"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231656" label="[23:16:56]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">not really a blocker for bootstrap</span></div><div class="line" id="231703"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231703" label="[23:17:03]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but I just patched it out</span></div><div class="line" id="231736"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231736" label="[23:17:36]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">3.0 and later ones had no issues at all...</span></div><div class="line" id="231751"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231751" label="[23:17:51]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">so overall not too bad</span></div><div class="line" id="231917"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231917" label="[23:19:17]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and this was tested on ruby git repo, so hopefully on other pregenerated files</span></div><div class="line" id="231920"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#231920" label="[23:19:20]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">and on a system  with no ruby</span></div><div class="line" id="234443"><span class="nick" style="color:#6d2462"><a href="#234443" label="[23:44:43]">&lt;kpcyrd&gt;</a></span><span class="message">hm, I think there was more context why I was asking this question. I remember it was very directly tied to whatsrc. but cool that you've figured it out!</span></div><div class="line" id="234602"><span class="nick" style="color:#6d2462"><a href="#234602" label="[23:46:02]">&lt;kpcyrd&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I think for a distro like Arch Linux it's eventually going to boil down to &quot;can you bootstrap it from the bootstrappable-builds distro&quot;</span></div><div class="line" id="234832"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#234832" label="[23:48:32]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it might have been in the hindsight of xz</span></div><div class="line" id="234838"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#234838" label="[23:48:38]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">can we build directly from the repo...</span></div><div class="line" id="235050"><span class="nick" style="color:#6d2462"><a href="#235050" label="[23:50:50]">&lt;kpcyrd&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yes, but I forgot why ruby specifically</span></div><div class="line" id="235126"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#235126" label="[23:51:26]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">probably other things too, just ruby is one of them...</span></div><div class="line" id="235150"><span class="nick" style="color:#6d2462"><a href="#235150" label="[23:51:50]">&lt;kpcyrd&gt;</a></span><span class="message">since I don't really use it personally. might be due to something raised by some other Arch Linux person who was more involved with ruby (possibly anthraxx).</span></div><div class="line" id="235402"><span class="nick" style="color:#6d2462"><a href="#235402" label="[23:54:02]">&lt;kpcyrd&gt;</a></span><span class="message">anyway, cool to know it can be bootstrapped!</span></div><br /></div></body></html>